<div id="2026-11-09-inventoryaccounting-twiggy-unit" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-09 — InventoryAccounting :4001 starts under Twiggy</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> A worktree entry in <code>root/config/worktrees.json</code> may now set <code>"twiggy": true</code>; <code>script/autostart/gen_branch_units.pl</code> then writes <code>-w</code> into that unit's <code>ExecStart</code> and stamps the reason into the unit header. <code>InventoryAccounting</code> (port 4001) is the first entry to use it. The generator also gained <code>--only=BRANCH</code> so one unit can be rewritten without touching the other 15.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> Without <code>-w</code> the server is <code>Catalyst::ScriptRunner</code>, which never loads <code>script/comserv_server.psgi</code>. That costs two things: no WebSocket, so the browser terminal stays disabled (<code>_interactive_ws_available</code> keys off <code>COMSERV_TWIGGY</code>/Twiggy server software), and none of the PSGI middleware runs (trusted-proxy <code>X-Forwarded-For</code>, <code>PortlessHost</code>, static MIME/APK header fixes). Static files were being served by <code>Catalyst::Plugin::Static::Simple</code> instead.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>script/autostart/gen_branch_units.pl</code>. The <code>"twiggy": true</code> flag is in <code>root/config/worktrees.json</code>, which is excluded from git, so that flag does not travel with the merge. The regenerated unit file lives under <code>~/.config/systemd/user</code>, also outside git.</p>
</div>
